.Dd July 8, 2026
.Dt NEW_CONTAINER 8
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm new_container
.Nd create a new container (jail) on top of an existing foundation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl s Ar name
.Op Fl f Ar foundation
.Op Fl o Ar key=value
.Op Fl q
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility creates a new container (jail) based on an existing foundation.
It mirrors
.Xr new_system 8
but produces a jail managed by
.Xr jail 8
instead of a bootable system.
.Pp
.Nm
creates a minhag directory containing a
.Xr jail.conf 5
skeleton, allocates data datasets, and makes an inaugural commit on a
container-specific branch.
Containers do not use
.Xr nextboot 8 ;
start them with
.Xr jail 8
instead.
.Pp
A foundation reference is recorded as a zero-byte file named
.Pa Ao Ar foundation Ac Ns .foundation
in the container's minhag directory, tying the container to the base
build it derives from.
.Pp
.Nm
operates in three modes:
.Bl -tag -width "Semi-interactive"
.It Em Interactive
When
.Fl s
is not given, the user is prompted for all configuration values.
.It Em Semi-interactive
When
.Fl s
is given without
.Fl q ,
the user is prompted for configuration values, with any
.Fl o
overrides offered as defaults.
.It Em Quiet
When both
.Fl s
and
.Fl q
are given, no prompts are issued.
Specifying
.Fl q
twice additionally suppresses progress output.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-f foundation"
.It Fl h
Display usage information and exit.
.It Fl d
Dry run.
Show what would be done without making changes.
.It Fl s Ar name
Set the container name.
Required when running in quiet mode.
.It Fl f Ar foundation
Foundation to base the container on.
The named foundation must already exist.
.It Fl o Ar key=value
Override a container configuration key.
May be specified multiple times.
Recognized keys:
.Bl -tag -width "mount_map" -compact
.It Cm home_dataset
Create a dedicated home dataset.
Default:
.Li yes .
.It Cm tmp_dataset
Create a dedicated tmp dataset.
Default:
.Li yes .
.It Cm user_homes
Comma-separated list of user home directories to provision under the
home dataset.
.It Cm mount_map
Additional dataset-to-mountpoint mapping in
.Ar dataset : Ns Ar mountpoint
form.
May be specified multiple times.
.El
.It Fl q
Quiet mode.
Suppress interactive prompts; requires
.Fl s .
When specified twice
.Pq Fl qq ,
progress output is also suppressed.
.El
.Sh EXECUTION FLOW
.Nm
proceeds through the following stages:
.Bl -enum
.It
Collect the container name, foundation, and configuration.
.It
Create the minhag directory at
.Pa minhag/containers/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /
with the following files:
.Xr jail.conf 5
skeleton,
.Pa compose.sh ,
.Pa derivations.local ,
.Pa fstab.local ,
.Pa mtree.dist ,
and
.Pa pkg.list .
.It
Write a zero-byte
.Pa Ao Ar foundation Ac Ns .foundation
file recording the foundation reference.
.It
Create data datasets under
.Pa zbamidbar/container\-data/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /
for
.Pa var ,
.Pa usr\-local ,
and optionally
.Pa home
and
.Pa tmp .
.It
Make an inaugural commit on the
.Li container/ Ns Ar name
branch on
.Pa zbamidbar/sinai.git
with
.Pa /etc/fstab
entries for the data datasets.
.It
Deploy the container to
.Pa zbereshit/containers/ Ns Ar name .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "zbamidbar/container-data/<name>/"
.It Pa minhag/containers/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /.foundation
Zero-byte file whose name records the foundation this container
derives from.
.It Pa minhag/containers/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /jail.conf
.Xr jail.conf 5
skeleton for the container.
.It Pa minhag/containers/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /compose.sh
Composition script controlling derivation application.
.It Pa minhag/containers/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /derivations.local
Local derivation list for the container.
.It Pa minhag/containers/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /fstab.local
Local fstab overrides.
.It Pa minhag/containers/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /mtree.dist
.Xr mtree 8
specification for the container's file hierarchy.
.It Pa minhag/containers/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /pkg.list
Package list for the container.
.It Pa zbamidbar/container\-data/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /
Parent dataset for container-specific persistent data, containing
.Pa var ,
.Pa usr\-local ,
.Pa home ,
and
.Pa tmp
child datasets.
.It Pa zbamidbar/sinai.git
Bare repository holding the
.Li container/ Ns Ar name
branch with the inaugural commit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a container interactively:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# new_container
.Ed
.Pp
Create a container on a specific foundation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# new_container -s webjail -f prod15
.Ed
.Pp
Create a container with user homes provisioned:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# new_container -s devjail -f prod15 -o user_homes=alice,bob
.Ed
.Pp
Fully automated creation with no prompts:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# new_container -s buildjail -f prod15 -q
.Ed
.Pp
Preview what a quiet creation would do:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# new_container -s buildjail -f prod15 -d -q
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr new_system 8 ,
.Xr new_foundation 8 ,
.Xr deploy_system 8 ,
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr jail.conf 5
